{
  "case_id": "2012-12-71",
  "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "House committee",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The House committee which dealt with the very act that -- that we have said, \"Only the elected officials designated and authorized under State law are charged with responsibility to enroll eligible voters on the list of voters. The NVRA should not be interpreted in any way to supplant that authority. The committee is particularly interested in ensuring that election officials continue to make determinations as to applicants' eligibility, such as citizenship, as they're made under current law and practice.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FEC",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the FEC, which is a predecessor to the EAC, relying on that House committee report, said that an application received by a local voter registration official is only an application and be subject to whatever verification procedures are currently applied to all applications."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what use does Arizona make of that attestation under perjury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "making of the Federal provision that's there in the form: I am a citizen. What use are you making of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, could -- could I take you back to this distinction that you're making."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you fit in the question of what documents you use to prove that with establishing the qualification? Meaning citizenship,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court found that 31,550 people were rejected from voting because of Proposition 200."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is all that stuff required by the Vote America Act? All that stuff?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Commission divided by a vote of 2-2."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Srinivasan)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the statute -- the statute seeks to streamline registration, but it's not an objective to the exclusion of all other objectives. And the EAC is charged with balancing the various competing statutory objectives. And it concluded in \u2013 with respect to the Louisiana submission -- that that one was okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the statute presupposes that the State can conduct its own investigation to crosscheck the information that the individual supplies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask you a question that I asked Ms. Millett? Does the United States think that the Arizona form is illegal? And if it is not, what sense does it make to have a system in which whether or not someone will successfully register depends on the happenstance of the particular form that the person fills out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Horne)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- my friend says in discussing Section 7(b)(1) that it would not be rational to require only the signature. But that's exactly what they did. All they required was the signature, and 7(b)(1) has nothing to do with that; 7(b)(2) requires a signature. So what the EAC chose to do under 7(b)(1) was exactly nothing, zero, which -- which emphasizes the point that this is the responsibility of the States, and that's how they understood it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-71",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05eeb1baaf2243d1909fb15e336b0abefa0445b2b12e8de41c164f63a0327dd8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05eeb1baaf22-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:08 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
